`md list` prints an ABSOLUTE path in every record, and the harness runs each
case in a scratch directory whose name is random, so a line holding a path can
never be pinned byte for byte. Cases that list at least one file therefore pipe
the output through `md lines`, which selects the lines that hold no path.

broken.md opens a YAML flow sequence and never closes it, so its frontmatter
cannot be read. The README says a parse error is reported and the run CONTINUES,
and broken.md sorts before zeta.md, so zeta.md is the proof: its `title` line is
still printed, giving one line plus the final newline, which `md lines --count`
reports as 2. A run that gave up at broken.md would report 1.

--key is used rather than the plain listing so that this case does not also
depend on how the broken file itself is rendered. That is pinned separately by
list-plain-does-not-report-broken-frontmatter-as-empty.
